    "title": "Lynx take down Liberty in first rematch of last season's WNBA Finals - NewsBreak",
    "text": "It took a long time for the WNBA Finals rematch between the Lynx and Liberty to happen, but it finally did Wednesday in Minneapolis and Minnesota stayed nearly perfect at home with a 100-93 victory. The Lynx are now 15-1 at Target Center this season, and the win gets them to 23-5 overall. That's four games ahead of the Liberty, who own the WNBA's second-best record at 17-9. Minnesota received a championship effort from Napheesa Collier , who finished with 30 points on 11-of-16 shooting to go along with nine rebounds and three blocks. Kayla McBride gave the Lynx 24 points and led the team with five three-pointers. As a team, the Lynx were on-fire from deep, knocking down 15 of 31 threes. Sabrina Ionescu led New York with 31 points. The Lynx and Liberty will meet three more times this season, and they'll happen in succession on Aug. 10th, 16th and 19th.",
